WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:04.000
Spend now follows payback, and a
person approves every budget move.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.633
Now the same discipline for
what you know about an account.

00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:09.867
A sourced brief on any account,
re-checked on a schedule,

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:11.367
and nothing taken on faith.

00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:14.033
By the end you'll know how to
request a brief and read the queue.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:17.733
You'll decide what research suggests,
and see where the findings go.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.133
Mia preps the night before a renewal call.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:22.133
She pastes what she finds into a note.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:25.633
Three weeks later the champion has
left, the note still names her,

00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:28.467
and nobody has looked again.
A note is a photograph.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.600
You need a researcher who keeps looking.

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.700
First, tell research who you are,

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.267
or a brief can't say why
an account matters to you.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.867
GTM OS reads your company
site into a workspace profile,

00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:42.700
and every brief frames an account
against what you actually sell.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.633
In the console: CRM, Research, settings.

00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:47.833
Or ask your agent: "Refresh
our workspace profile".

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:51.400
You'll see the profile
re-read, with what changed.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.700
Read it before briefs rely on it, and
refresh it whenever your site changes.

00:00:55.733 --> 00:01:00.233
Second, ask for a brief, so one request
replaces an evening of open tabs.

00:01:00.233 --> 00:01:04.000
In the console: CRM, Accounts, open
the account, and choose Research.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.567
Or ask your agent: "Research Northwind".

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.967
The task joins a queue and
runs in the background.

00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:13.033
When it finishes, the
brief lands on the account,

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.800
and every line carries its source:
a careers page, a news article.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.100
Research draws on web search,
page extraction, news,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.467
and the person and company
enrichment you have bound.

00:01:23.533 --> 00:01:28.433
Third, watch the queue, so a failed
lookup shows up instead of vanishing.

00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:30.567
In the console: CRM, Research, queue.

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:33.433
Or ask your agent: "What
is in the research queue".

00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:37.733
Each task reads running, queued,
failed, or scheduled for a re-check.

00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:40.667
Retry a failed one, or
cancel one that's running.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:44.533
Your agent lists tasks by state,
with the next re-check date.

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:47.833
Now what keeps a brief fresh:
time. Briefs don't rot.

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:51.000
Re-checks follow how much a
contact matters: by default,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.533
champions every fourteen days,
named contacts every ninety,

00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:57.300
and people research
couldn't find, once a year.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.633
Before a meeting, a brief
older than a week is refreshed.

00:02:00.633 --> 00:02:04.767
A daily budget caps the spend, and
once it's gone, queued tasks wait.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.900
The second mechanism is
why a fact deserves trust.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.300
Research reports observations,
never a confidence.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.933
Each kind has a fixed weight,
and independent signals combine.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.133
On its own, a search result stays weak.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.067
A fact only reaches verified
with a primary source:

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:22.000
a profile that names the
employer, an email signature,

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.200
or a reply on a thread
your mailbox synced.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.300
If another value has real support, the
fact waits for a person to settle it.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.467
Every fact carries its source, and
a weak source never counts as proof.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.767
Fourth, decide what counts. In the
console: CRM, Research, suggestions.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.600
Each one shows its source,
and you accept or dismiss it.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.100
Or ask your agent: "Accept the
funding fact for Northwind".

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.767
It will send you to the console,
because deciding is human only.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:49.867
Mind this: read the
source before you accept.

00:02:49.867 --> 00:02:52.500
A value you dismiss is
never offered again.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.667
Research never overwrites
something a person typed,

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:58.267
and an employer change
never applies on its own.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:02.400
Accepted facts resolve to the record
that exists, so you don't get a twin.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:03.867
Now where the findings go.

00:03:03.867 --> 00:03:06.333
One to one drafts read the
brief for their opening,

00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:09.767
so a first touch can mention
something true and recent.

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.600
The meeting prep play builds a brief

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.600
and a prep task before a meeting starts.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.133
Accepted facts can also feed scoring.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:18.000
Ask your agent: "What do
we know about Northwind".

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.467
You get the brief, the accepted
facts, the open suggestions,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.133
and the date of the last check.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.733
Settings choose the sources, the
re-check rhythm and the limits.

00:03:26.733 --> 00:03:29.800
In the console: CRM, Research, settings.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.200
Or ask your agent: "Show
the research settings".

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.067
Changes happen in the console.
Then open Operate, Cost.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.967
Each brief can use paid lookups,

00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:39.767
so the ledger shows what one
account cost to research.

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:42.833
Pro move: keep the daily
budget low in week one.

00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:46.100
After a week of ledger lines
you know what a brief costs,

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.267
and you raise the budget on purpose.

00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:51.433
It improves in two ways.
Re-checks keep briefs current,

00:03:51.433 --> 00:03:54.333
and your accept and dismiss
decisions keep the record clean.

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:58.100
To customize: bindings choose
which sources research may use,

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:02.100
the workspace profile frames what you
sell, and settings set the rhythm.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:05.133
Fair concern: an agent
writing facts into my CRM?

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:08.167
It can request and read, but
it can't decide a suggestion,

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:09.533
because that's human only.

00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.800
Nor can it turn on automatic
acceptance of verified facts.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.033
And every applied fact keeps its source
and its band, with an audit entry.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:20.533
Know the edge. Research works
one account or contact at a time.

00:04:20.533 --> 00:04:22.233
It isn't account based marketing,

00:04:22.233 --> 00:04:24.933
and it doesn't run sales
intelligence across your market.

00:04:24.933 --> 00:04:26.367
Those aren't built yet.

00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:30.533
Replay: Your profile says who you are.
The queue re-checks on a schedule.

00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:33.367
Facts carry their source
until a person decides.

00:04:33.433 --> 00:04:35.933
Any account can have a sourced
brief that stays fresh.

00:04:35.933 --> 00:04:38.800
Open one account and
request a brief today.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.300
Coming next: Plays and Studio,
where automations run on your rules,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.900
after you've simulated them.
